  "contract": [
    "A seek opens a preloaded seekable input and creates the demuxer; after EOF, it first reads and folds every packet through confirmed end of file. It then seeks backward on one track to a time in that track's media clock: the candidate through compat::mov::seek::GlobalSeekJob, the reference through its public backward seek (av_seek_frame with AVSEEK_FLAG_BACKWARD). It reads and folds up to the requested number of packets, at most 64, collects stream and program metadata and closes the demuxer.",
    "A range plan opens the same input with strict tables and complete media; after EOF, it first reads every track's samples to the end. It plans a source seek on one track with MovieSourceSeekPlanner and published roll recovery, the requested time taken as movie time, and reads and folds the plan's samples from its decode start through its target, each from its source range. The reference does the equivalent work: the same backward seek, then reading as many packets as the plan holds.",
    "Input loading, SHA-256 proof, process startup and output serialization are outside the measured operation. Rewind, parser and index allocation, the read to end of file, the seek or plan, packet or sample delivery with payload reads, folding and teardown are inside.",
    "Seek traces must be byte-identical and reproduce their expected packet, byte and digest counts. A range plan matches when it is complete and its samples and the reference's packets after the seek have the requested count, the requested track and the same source positions, sizes and payloads in order, the reference stopping at its delivery limit. Each role's work is then its own recorded fold, with the same packets and bytes.",
    "Ordinary windows are 65536 bytes with a work quantum of 4096; tiny windows are one byte with a quantum of three, on open and index corpus inputs only. Both use preloaded input and zero retained packets.",
    "The 476 cases read 44 inputs: eight authored movies (harness/fixtures/isobmff-seek, written by cargo xtask isobmff-seek fixtures) and inputs of the open and index corpus. Authored movies are sought on every track at the start, one tick before a sync sample, at it, seven samples after it and beyond the end, fresh and after EOF, and read for one packet after a non-sync landing; their single-track movies are planned at the same sync points and at the last sample. Corpus inputs are sought on their first track at the start, the middle and beyond the end, fresh, after EOF and in tiny windows, and range-planned at the middle and the last sample.",
    "378 seeks and 94 range plans are timed and measured. 4 explicit refusals, inputs whose open both workers refuse, are parity outcomes and are never timed.",
    "Not compared: seeks the candidate refuses as unsupported (a global seek across tracks with unequal clocks, overlapping or null index clocks, no observed key fallback, regular table recovery), seeks whose traces differ from the reference's, range plans on inputs with more than one track, and range plans that are not planned or differ.",
    "Expected work preserves the reference input SHA-256 and work-contract digest. Reference proof fields are checked separately from the candidate work projection."
  ],
